@@ -179,6 +179,7 @@ Some features are not supported in AdvCiv-SAS; e.g., non-English languages, pre-
 - **First city logic:** settlers consider a larger no-penalty scouting radius for founding the capital (`CvUnitAI::AI_foundFirstCity`), and no longer auto-reject non-coastal/non-river sites if a worse "preferred" site exists. It’ll just pick the **best** overall site. See [KI#43](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#43---attemptingly-improvedenhanced-ai-settlers-for-the-first-city-found-ie-at-turn-0-if-i-am-not-mistaken-settling-too-soon-instead-of-digging-a-bit-for-better-sites-and-other-related-changes).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5920+) **First-city roaming**: Since the first city is especially important, unlike later cities that can be more strategic or semi-decent resource grabs, starting settlers can now **roam briefly for a better first-city site when the current site is bad enough**. This uses a heuristic **BFC bad-plot count** so settlers can move away from clearly bad capital sites without making decent starts wander needlessly, like a human player would: settlers can now spend the bounded early window to **move to visible good-enough sites**, do **safe adjacent scouting for better information**, or **wait if no safe scouting step exists**. Bad plots include no-yield plots, bad water, no-bonus foodless hills (so not hill grassland for example as of now), and no-bonus low-food flat land, while seafood, useful bonus tiles, grass hills, high-yield plots, and workable water are preserved. Empirically, this is notably especially effective in moving away from bad tundra/plain no-bonus heavy starts for the first city.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5921+) **First-city recheck after scouting**: **instead of settling the first good-enough** capital site found **after leaving a very bad start**, the **settler now runs first-city evaluation again** on **nearby visible plots** including **now newly visible** ones first, like a human player would. Empirically, this helped choose even stronger nearby capital sites with more food bonuses and/or river support rather than stopping at the first merely-no-longer-bad site. As of now this applies only to the first city, because as of now only the first city is deemed most needing it critically, and later settlers usually know more of the local map so they would generally have a lower need to change route midway (may create other issues too maybe). See [KI#144](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#144---fixed-base-advciv-issue-and-advciv-sas-settler-free-window-follow-up-ai-settlers-sometimes-do-not-move-away-from-a-high-bad-plot-count-start-eg-high-non-bonus-tundra-and-plains-they-now-scout-and-hunt-for-better-not-very-bad-sites-and-no-longer-stop-at-first-good-enough-site-but-instead-now-rerun-evaluate-city-site-again-on-newly-visible-plots-if-a-better-site-eg-more-foodriversfresh-water-exists-nearby-which-we-now-value-more-too-for-first-city-as-well).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5928+) **Naval-heavy-map coastal settling:** On naval-heavy (e.g., Archipelago) maps, settler AI site valuation now optionally add **extra valuation for coastal sites**, as of now especially for the **first city**. This helps early work boat, scouting/contact, trade, first galleys, Moai, or other water-focused buildings; e.g., Cuzco needed a high first-city coastal extra valuation to prefer a coastal Pig + Banana + 2-Sugar river site over a central 4-Sugar river grass site; and kept **moderate for other cities** than the capital after testing showed higher values could, for example, overpull Japan toward tundra coast instead of grass. See [KI#146](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#146---fixedenhanced-base-advciv-issue-of-ai-undervaluing-coastal-settling-on-naval-heavy-maps).
 - **Parking addressed (early game):** Reduced cases of settlers idling in the capital despite safe/urgent expansion, by updating `CvUnitAI::AI_found` to found sooner when conditions allow. In autoplay samples, Spain shifted from **1 city @T100** to **~2 by T60–70** and **~3 by T80–90** (settler production varies somehow, but we move much sooner after we have it now). See [KI#68](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#68---tremendously-improved-ai-having-a-settler-parked-from-turn---45-to-turn-100-and-still-didnt-found-any-city-fixedaddressed-in-cvunitaiai_found).
 
